articles.content_en:
Any entity or individual engaging in securities and futures investment consultancy business within the territory of the People's Republic of China shall comply with these Measures.
For the purposes of these Measures, "securities and futures investment consultancy" refers to the activities in which institutions engaged in securities and futures investment consultancy business and their investment consultants provide securities and futures investors or clients with securities and futures investment analysis, forecasts or suggestions and other direct or indirect paid consultancy services in the following forms:
(1) accepting the entrustment of investors or clients to provide securities and futures investment consultancy services;
(2) holding lectures, seminars, analysis meetings, etc. on securities and futures investment consultancy;
(3) publishing articles, comments and reports on securities and futures investment consultancy in newspapers and periodicals, and providing securities and futures investment consultancy services through public media such as radio and television stations;
(4) providing securities and futures investment consultancy services through telecommunication equipment systems such as telephones, faxes and computer networks;
(5) other forms recognized by the China Securities Regulatory Commission (hereinafter referred to as the CSRC).

An institution applying for the qualification to engage in securities and futures investment consultancy shall meet the following conditions:
(1) An institution that separately engages in securities or futures investment consultancy business shall have at least five full-time persons who have obtained the qualification for securities and futures investment consultancy; an institution that concurrently engages in both securities and futures investment consultancy business shall have at least ten full-time persons who have obtained the qualification for securities and futures investment consultancy; among its senior officers, at least one person shall have obtained the qualification for securities or futures investment consultancy;
(2) having a registered capital of not less than RMB 1 million yuan;
(3) having a fixed business place and communication and other information transmission facilities appropriate to the business;
(4) having articles of association;
(5) having a sound internal management system;
(6) meeting other conditions required by the CSRC.

An institution applying for the qualification to engage in securities and futures investment consultancy shall be examined and approved according to the following procedures:
(1) The applicant shall submit an application to the local regulatory office (CSRC) authorized by the CSRC (if the local regulatory office (CSRC) is not authorized by the CSRC, the applicant shall directly submit an application to the CSRC, the same below); after examination and consent, the local regulatory office (CSRC) shall issue a preliminary examination opinion;
(2) The local regulatory office (CSRC) shall submit the application documents that have been examined and approved to the CSRC; after examination and approval by the CSRC, a business license shall be issued to the applicant, and the approval document shall be copied to the local regulatory office (CSRC);
(3) The CSRC shall publicly announce the circumstances of the applicants who have obtained the business license.

An institution applying for the qualification to engage in securities and futures investment consultancy shall submit the following documents:
(1) an application form uniformly printed by the CSRC;
(2) the articles of association;
(3) the business license for enterprise legal person;
(4) the list of senior officers and persons engaged in securities and futures investment consultancy business of the institution, together with their academic qualifications, work experience and qualification certificates;
(5) the methods of carrying out investment consultancy business and the internal management rules and regulations;
(6) the certificate of use of business premises, the institution's communication address, telephone number and fax number;
(7) the capital verification report provided by a certified public accountant;
(8) other documents required by the CSRC.

A securities and futures investment consultancy institution shall apply to the local regulatory office (CSRC) for annual inspection during the period from January 1 to April 30 each year. When applying for annual inspection, it shall submit the following documents:
(1) the annual inspection application report;
(2) the annual business report;
(3) the financial accounting statements audited by a certified public accountant.
The local regulatory office (CSRC) shall, within 20 working days from the date of receipt of the documents listed in the preceding paragraph, issue an examination opinion on the annual inspection application; if the application is approved upon examination, it shall be submitted to the CSRC for examination and approval.
A securities and futures investment consultancy institution that fails to submit the annual inspection report within the time limit or fails to pass the annual inspection after examination shall not continue to engage in securities and futures investment consultancy business.

A securities and futures investment consultant applying for obtaining the qualification for securities and futures investment consultancy shall meet the following conditions:
(1) having the nationality of the People's Republic of China;
(2) having full capacity for civil conduct;
(3) being of good conduct, honest and upright, and having good professional ethics;
(4) having not been subjected to criminal punishment or a serious administrative penalty related to securities or futures business;
(5) having a university bachelor's degree or above;
(6) a securities investment consultant having at least two years of experience in securities business, and a futures investment consultant having at least two years of experience in futures business;
(7) passing the securities and futures practitioners qualification examination uniformly organized by the CSRC;
(8) other conditions prescribed by the CSRC.

A securities and futures investment consultant applying for obtaining the qualification for securities and futures investment consultancy shall be examined and approved according to the following procedures:
(1) The applicant shall submit an application to the local regulatory office (CSRC) authorized by the CSRC (if the local regulatory office (CSRC) is not authorized by the CSRC, the applicant shall directly submit an application to the CSRC, the same below); after examination and consent, the local regulatory office (CSRC) shall issue a preliminary examination opinion;
(2) The local regulatory office (CSRC) shall submit the application documents that have been examined and approved to the CSRC; after examination and approval by the CSRC, a qualification certificate shall be issued to the applicant, and the approval document shall be copied to the local regulatory office (CSRC).

A securities and futures investment consultant applying for obtaining the qualification for securities and futures investment consultancy shall submit the following documents:
(1) an application form uniformly printed by the CSRC;
(2) an identity card;
(3) an academic qualification certificate;
(4) the transcript of the securities and futures practitioners qualification examination;
(5) a statement of past conduct issued by the applicant's work unit or the sub-district office of the place of household registration;
(6) other materials required by the CSRC.

Securities and futures investment consulting institutions and their investment consultants shall not engage in the following activities:
(1) acting as agent for investors in securities and futures trading;
(2) promising securities and futures investment returns to investors;
(3) agreeing with investors to share investment returns or bear investment losses;
(4) purchasing or selling stocks and securities with the nature and functions of stocks, as well as futures for their own account;
(5) using consulting services to collude with others to manipulate the market or engage in insider trading;
(6) other securities and futures fraudulent activities prohibited by laws, regulations and rules.

Where a securities and futures investment consulting institution commits any of the following acts, it shall be fined not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan by the local securities regulatory office (CSRC); if the circumstances are serious, the local securities regulatory office (CSRC) shall report to the CSRC, and the CSRC shall impose a penalty of suspension or revocation of its business qualification:
(1) the documents and materials submitted to the securities regulatory department contain false statements or material omissions;
(2) fails to fulfill the reporting and annual inspection obligations as prescribed in these Measures;
(3) fails to go through the procedures for modification of changes in relevant circumstances of the institution as prescribed in these Measures;
(4) the securities and futures investment consultants of the institution violate the provisions of these Measures and are subject to administrative penalty by the securities regulatory department;
(5) interferes with or obstructs the inspection or investigation by the local securities regulatory office (CSRC), or conceals or destroys evidence.
